    "video_file_size": 5624196,
    "caption": "🤖 RealBOTs Take On Real Work\n\nChinese company RealMan Robotics plans to place almost 1,000 RealBOT units in workplaces in 2026. At WRC 2026 in Beijing, demos showed robots sorting medicines, inspecting a distribution switchboard, baking with human cooks, and handling remote equipment commissioning at the Changzhou factory.\n\nThe Global Link Network lets a human operator control the robot remotely, with claimed millisecond-level latency across thousands of kilometers. A scarce skill can reach the needed site without sending the specialist there.\n\nEach task produces data from unpredictable conditions. More work should make the robots better at working.\n\n📊@tech",
